.TH CENTCOM-UPDATE 1 "" "centcom 0.1.0 (contract 1.2.0)" "Centcom"
.SH NAME
centcom\-update \- look for a newer Centcom and bring it in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B centcom update [\-\-check] [\-\-channel stable|beta|nightly] [\-\-yes] [\-\-allow\-downgrade] [\-\-rollback] [\-\-json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Looks for a newer release on your channel, shows what it will do and asks first. Exit codes: 0 up to date or updated, 1 failed or cancelled, 2 bad options, 10 an update is available (with \-\-check), 11 verification failed, 12 this install cannot update itself (it shows the command to run).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
only look; exit 10 when something newer is available
.TP
.B \-\-channel <stable|beta|nightly>
follow another channel for this run
.TP
.B \-\-yes
do not ask before updating
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-downgrade
go to an older version on purpose
.TP
.B \-\-rollback
go back to the version you had before the last update
.TP
.B \-\-json
one JSON object instead of text
.SH SEE ALSO
centcom help, https://centcom.dev/docs
